# generated, never hand-committed
dist/
.ipynb_checkpoints/
# lesson.ipynb IS committed. It is generated from lesson.py by tools/notebooks.py, but it is
# also the artefact a student actually opens -- in Colab, Kaggle, Binder or local Jupyter --
# and a repository of notebooks that ships no notebooks helps nobody. `notebooks.py --check`
# fails the build if a committed .ipynb has drifted from the lesson.py it came from.
__pycache__/
*.pyc
# build products of the C/C++ lessons
*.o
*.dSYM/
lesson_bin
solutions/lesson_bin
# per-lesson build directories: binaries and generated test data. tools/execute.py deletes
# them before every run because a stale binary can point at a dead library path. 8.5 MiB of
# them (two Mach-O executables, six generated CSVs) were once committed by a `git add -A`.
build/
# environment
.venv/
.DS_Store
# iCloud Drive sync duplicates. This tree lives under ~/Documents, which iCloud syncs, and a
# build running while it syncs leaves copies named "lesson_bin 2", "assets 3" and so on. They
# are never wanted: the build products are ignored above and the asset directories are real.
lesson_bin [0-9]
assets [0-9]
*.o [0-9]
# NOTE: solutions/ and tests/ are deliberately NOT ignored. They are version-controlled and
# excluded from the student bundle by tools/build_student_bundle.py (QUALITY.md gate 7).
